# ROADMAP_NS_PV1 — Fail-closed user path vs SHIPPED claims

File: openOODA/audit/roadmap_ns_pv1.oot
Logline: Attacks user-facing SHIPPED claims that are not oodac leftover and not library leftover.
Setup: Survey only. No product edit. No ROADMAP edit. C emit + gcc remains the product path.
Beats:
  1. Hunt the door, registry, HITL, vscode, qa_master, fix/patch, ingest.
  2. Compare each claim to disk and to NORTHSTAR 1.1.
  3. Recommend an open row only for a stranger lie or an unproved SHIPPED claim.

## 0. Scope

  Residual in ROADMAP 5.1 stays residual. Do not open a row to build
  the installer, HITL, vscode JS, or `qa/e2e/*.sh`.
  Do not reopen ROADMAP section 6 stale words.
  Do not open oodac leftover (5.3) or library leftover (5.4).
  Do not open moonshots.
  Production here means NORTHSTAR 1.1, a fail-closed hole, or a lie
  a stranger meets on the pin.

## 1. NORTHSTAR 1.1 vs SHIPPED

  Early static check: SHIPPED names const header fold. Full SMT is residual.
  SHIPPED does not treat 1.1 as done. Open: no.
  Zero ambient authority: user effects need tokens. SHIPPED names the jail.
  CLI host still uses `sh -c` for curl, git, and minisign. That is the host
  driver, not a user binary. Open: no.
  Determinism: SHIPPED names emit-c byte match. gcc binaries stay residual
  (OPEN-71 in the closed log). SHIPPED does not treat binary outputs as done.
  Open: no.
  Agent tools: JSON check, outline, reflect, fix, patch are on disk.
  Open: no.
  High performance / SoA: not a user command. Do not open a moonshot.

## 2. Hits

### H1 Door sells first-machine bootstrap

  Claim: `curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install | oo` plus a list of
  paths under `~/.local/bin` and `~/.local/share/ooda/`.
  NORTHSTAR: none. WORKFLOW 0.1 and ROADMAP 5.1: do not sell this as
  a first-machine bootstrap.
  Disk: `openOODA.github.io/install` prints three lines and exits.
  It does not write binaries. `ooda/cli/cmd_more.oo` `ooda install`
  prints `ooda install: ok` and copies nothing.
  Site README still names `| sh` and `install.sh`. There is no `install.sh`.
  Guide/Use.oot says the one-liner is paused. The door does not.
  Production requirement? yes (stranger lie on the pin).
  Recommend open row? yes.

### H2 Registry sold as a finished store

  Claim: `ooda add hello --registry https://registry.openooda.org`
  is the public store. Guide Home, Packages, Options, and
  `registry/index.html` sell that line.
  NORTHSTAR: 1.1 agent tooling only. ROADMAP 6 remaining text:
  do not sell a finished first-machine store.
  Disk: `registry/catalog` has five names (hello, mid, world, evilcap,
  tooyank). Fetch and minisign exist (`cli/cmd_pm_reg.oo`,
  `qa/pm_reg_spine.oo`, `cli/pm_reg_proof.oo`). This is a demo vendor.
  It is not a first-machine store. Install is paused, so a stranger
  has no `ooda` to run `--registry`.
  `registry/README.oot` still says the CLI does not fetch the host.
  That sentence is stale. The CLI does fetch.
  Production requirement? yes (stranger lie on the pin).
  Recommend open row? yes.

### H3 HITL claimed as product

  Claim: Guide Use.oot calls `ooda fix` the human HITL loop and
  points at research RP-5-6.
  NORTHSTAR: none. SHIPPED: HITL is not product. The human loop is
  `ooda fix`. ROADMAP 5.1 same.
  Disk: `ooda fix` is product. RP-5-6 names attestation caps, signed
  traces, and a native pause. Those files are not product.
  Production requirement? no (5.1 residual; SHIPPED is honest).
  Recommend open row? no.

### H4 vscode claimed native-only

  Claim: `vscode/README.oot` sells official native `ooda lsp`.
  Feature bullets still say hover and definition use the first `fn`.
  NORTHSTAR: 1.1 agent tools. SHIPPED: vscode still talks to
  `vscode/server/ooda-lsp.js`. `ooda lsp` is a native loop.
  Disk: `extension.js` starts `ooda lsp`. `server/ooda-lsp.js` remains.
  `server/README.oot` still says the client targets the JS file.
  `scripts/lsp_cursor_smoke.oo` proves cursor hover on `ooda lsp`.
  Production requirement? no (5.1 residual; SHIPPED is honest).
  Recommend open row? no.

### H5 qa_master 22 green vs README suite

  Claim: SHIPPED says `qa_master.oo` prints `qa_master: PASSED` (22 green).
  `qa/README.oot` sells end-to-end, fuzz, regression, and a compliance suite.
  NORTHSTAR: none.
  Disk: `qa_master.oo` globs 22 files. Residual header names
  beh_02/06/07/08, ai_rec_02, conc/cross/fuzz, and `e2e/*.sh`.
  README table still lists those dirs as the suite.
  This survey did not run `ooda run ./qa_master.oo`.
  Production requirement? no (not the pin door; 5.1 residual).
  Recommend open row? no.

### H6 ooda fix / patch path refuse

  Claim: SHIPPED: absolute paths and symlinks refuse. Unset
  `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` denies. No TTY and no `--yes` refuses.
  NORTHSTAR: 1.1 automated repair.
  Disk: `cli/fix_text.oo` `path_bad` (`/` and `..`).
  `fix_util.oo` `refuse_symlink`. `patch_drive.oo` same.
  `write_file` uses `realpath` and `O_NOFOLLOW` (`chs_rt_fs.c`).
  Proof: `qa/write_gate_spine.oo`, `scripts/patch_smoke.oo`.
  Cited SHIPPED lock `emust_autofix_smoke.oo` does not cover path refuse.
  The refuse still lives on disk.
  Production requirement? no (proved).
  Recommend open row? no.

### H7 Ingest git allow-list

  Claim: SHIPPED: ingest refuses HTTP, git://, and userinfo lookalikes
  before clone.
  NORTHSTAR: 1.1 zero ambient authority (fetch).
  Disk: `cli/pm_allow.oo` + `cmd_pm_git.oo` check before `git clone`.
  Proof: `cli/pm_extract_proof.oo`, `qa/pm_allow_spine.oo`.
  `https://user:pass@github.com/...` is allowed. That is auth on a
  good host, not a lookalike.
  Production requirement? no (proved).
  Recommend open row? no.

